{
    "background_story": "Jensen was a brilliant mathematician who spent his career studying the intricacies of permutations. His fascination with the way elements could be rearranged to create new patterns and combinations led him to make groundbreaking discoveries in the field of combinatorics. Jensen's work on permutability had far-reaching implications, from cryptography to coding theory. He was particularly interested in the concept of derangements, where a permutation leaves no element in its original position. Jensen's research took him down many rabbit holes, but his passion for permutability remained constant. He became known for his ability to find innovative solutions to complex problems, often by rearranging seemingly unrelated concepts. Jensen's work continues to inspire new generations of mathematicians and computer scientists.",
